WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.559
With nestjs-i18n, each language
has a folder of JSON catalogs

2
00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:07.370
that you write.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.683
It does its part well,

4
00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:11.145
with language resolvers,

5
00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:13.165
typed keys, and plurals.

6
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.541
General Translation
translates the catalogs,

7
00:00:16.541 --> 00:00:19.373
and gt-node translates
runtime content.

8
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.367
Point the gt config at
the catalog folders,

9
00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.419
and run npx gt translate in CI.

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.982
Each run then translates
only what changed.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.751
For content your users write,

12
00:00:32.751 --> 00:00:36.512
gt-node translates at run
time in the same language.

13
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.529
Your team now ships
German with each release.
